{"user": "How does making 1 move mean the opponent can gain multiple disks", "user_ts": "2026-08-05T13:58:26.255661+00:00", "assistant": "Because in Othello, a move doesn\u2019t just place **1 new disc** \u2014 it also flips every opponent disc trapped in a line between the new disc and another of your discs.\n\nExample: if White plays and flips 4 Black discs:\n\n- White places 1 new disc: **+1 White**\n- Those 4 Black discs become White: **+4 White, -4 Black**\n\nSo the score difference swings by **9** discs:  \nWhite gains 5 total, Black loses 4.\n\nThat\u2019s why one move can suddenly change the count a lot, especially in the endgame.", "assistant_started_ts": "2026-08-05T13:58:35.723778+00:00", "assistant_ts": "2026-08-05T13:58:37.694306+00:00", "annotation_user": {"final": ["Knowledge Deficit Question"], "consensus": ["Knowledge Deficit Question"], "votes": {"Knowledge Deficit Question": 3}, "confidence": {"Knowledge Deficit Question": 1.0}, "per_model": {"gpt": ["Knowledge Deficit Question"], "llama": ["Knowledge Deficit Question"], "sonnet": ["Knowledge Deficit Question"]}, "n_valid": 3, "min_votes": 2, "no_majority": false, "needs_review": false, "arbiter_used": false}, "annotation_assistant": {"final": ["Direct Instruction"], "consensus": ["Direct Instruction"], "votes": {"Direct Instruction": 3}, "confidence": {"Direct Instruction": 1.0}, "per_model": {"gpt": ["Direct Instruction"], "llama": ["Direct Instruction"], "sonnet": ["Direct Instruction"]}, "n_valid": 3, "min_votes": 2, "no_majority": false, "needs_review": false, "arbiter_used": false}, "annotation_assistant_fine": {"final": ["General Principle"], "consensus": ["General Principle"], "votes": {"General Principle": 3}, "confidence": {"General Principle": 1.0}, "per_model": {"gpt": ["General Principle"], "llama": ["General Principle"], "sonnet": ["General Principle"]}, "n_valid": 3, "min_votes": 2, "no_majority": false, "needs_review": false, "arbiter_used": false, "coarse": ["Direct Instruction"]}